esGo6AC4BU3EHjoi_C6skDxNdugD3MdwC4TTs4_UL-PW8D8GCyMZIN6Rq16pgeCRkaIuRfL496dH29DW0Sb-BQlzaHIx2YwUK7wJLAVCm-GTD4YX-zcmu7p_Q4aZxdG6o8RH7FK3lXi5t9FCGWtHvqAMvneAvlB-H9AkwEyKOsiFDReifGi4mUXkVPe9877M0mjL0xx_EG61nFTzUkY_np4Nipr4ffIfmT2hIcztf28H9fknU2IMPMouQ9RI4us2VPO_-bG59bxe32qvWHih_5wUzDNpuJ9e25bki8sxk5Fvb4DYvE_DktGRDqm4j7jDX8KugtxKF2pCPnXCBQIp6lZ4yFjynm9n-uu6Bk9pk9gOlTCijRyeosnctlEyxaZSldn75iSVDTkP37Hdde6HSQI1hZdor85EnRBgMHBkhqFVY0gTK6el4PnZAKZwYZXJ17KxVv7DoKORT4Bbiz6AdihNlQVh6WDoFkIsD630AzgDkBHWpbt9ooJkthVwNImPekBiMlXF4tZF5LWSitgMRnCWowREItDFCcKqDjp5kIqtGKe1XECKB-QbU4aXbLp7d_mVvij5sHoxJetGTFexoGLZYmO0UTINQdmzcp58PdhWps1MrJZC_CTbQNNTsnnqrcWt1BvtCD2yfb7-A6fbFwYn0m20NTNtO1MZvgcWNSH-PXnZAWCQ4zynGqBf5iMaR3_alsPs8dk_YNY1NiFWjm4KRuAU4pOpkeUT93ur05om4ieoRPxWvTDkeg5MH1fXxYhjuYx9rklif07D5pEnWfB1lXPgd54KwEpf_FojlLJHt6u6Bw="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0512108438a84476016adb5845a59c8191ba438a1e82308819","call_id":"call_05677ff54494457b81873a3da852d647","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped TensorProduct\\nnoncomputable def dividedPower (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] (f : V →ₗ[ℂ] V) (r : ℕ) : V →ₗ[ℂ] V := ((Nat.factorial r : ℂ)⁻¹) • (f ^ r)\\nnoncomputable def tensorAction {K : Type*} [Field K] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (f : M →ₗ[ℤ] M) : K ⊗[ℤ] M →ₗ[K] K ⊗[ℤ] M := TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f\\ndef InvariantUnder (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (f : E →ₗ[K] E) (W : Submodule K E) : Prop := ∀ z ∈ W, f z ∈ W\\ndef LieIrreducible (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (x y z : E →ₗ[K] E) : Prop := Nontrivial E ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K E, InvariantUnder K E x W → InvariantUnder K E y W → InvariantUnder K E z W → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\\nstructure LieLatticeData (lam : ℤ) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] where\\n  V : Type\\n  [vAdd : AddCommGroup V]\\n  [vMod : Module ℂ V]\\n  basisV : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℂ V\\n  basisM : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℤ M\\n  embed : M →ₗ[ℤ] V\\n  x : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  y : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  z : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  xM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  yM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  zM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  v : V\\nnoncomputable def LieLatticeData.H004 {lam : ℤ} {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (D : LieLatticeData lam M) : Prop := by\\n  letI := D.vAdd\\n  letI := D.vMod\\n  exact (∀ i, D.basisV i = D.embed (D.basisM i)) ∧ Function.Injective D.embed ∧\\n    (∀ w, D.z (D.x w) - D.x (D.z w) = (2:ℂ) • D.x w) ∧\\n    (∀ w, D.z (D.y w) - D.y (D.z w) = (-2:ℂ) • D.y w) ∧\\n    (∀ w, D.x (D.y w) - D.y (D.x w) = D.z w) ∧ D.v ≠ 0 ∧ D.x D.v = 0 ∧ D.z D.v = (lam:ℂ) • D.v ∧\\n    (∀ m, D.embed (D.xM m) = D.x (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.yM m) = D.y (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ m, D.embed (D.zM m) = D.z (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.z\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"LieLatticeData lam M\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0 : ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p : ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"LieLatticeData.H004 D\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (K ⊗[ℤ] M) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.zM)\",\"representation\":\"Reuses the previous arbitrary-lattice encoding: M is a free ℤ-module with basis, injectively embedded as a ℤ-lattice in the complex highest-weight space V, with the complex operators and their compatible integral restrictions; divided powers preserve the embedded lattice. The target carrier is K ⊗[ℤ] M, with K acting on the first factor, and x,y,h act by the induced maps. The source presentation is M ⊗[ℤ] K; TensorProduct.comm gives the canonical underlying tensor commutor. This plan records a specific bridge obligation rather than treating the commutor as a comment. Nevertheless the final target here remains the K-first presentation and requires source-fidelity review.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"∀ i : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), True\",\"inputs\":[\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\"],\"explanation\":\"Establish the divided-power basis, eigenvalue separation over ℂ, termination at both ends, and the integral divided-power action formulas from the highest-weight relations. This proposition is only a placeholder-sized signature and does not export those formulas; it is not a complete implementation of S001.\"},{\"id\":\"T002\",\"statement\":\"∀ i j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), True\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T001\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S002\"],\"explanation\":\"Use the formulas from S001 to calculate the matrix-unit composites, including the generally nonzero intermediate Y-power terms, and invert the binomial coefficient in Z_(p), including λ=0 and p=2.\"},{\"id\":\"T003\",\"statement\":\"True\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T002\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S003\"],\"explanation\":\"Analyze the arbitrary localized lattice coordinate modules, finite freeness and torsion-freeness; compute the scalar-extension dimension before proving rank one, then clear denominators and use the valuation argument to obtain a generator.\"},{\"id\":\"T004\",\"statement\":\"True\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T003\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S004\"],\"explanation\":\"Reduce the arbitrary lattice basis modulo p and extend scalars to K; identify the resulting basis and the x,y,h action matrices with the source M tensor_Z K construction.\"},{\"id\":\"T005\",\"statement\":\"True\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T002\",\"T004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S005\"],\"explanation\":\"Reduce matrix-unit identities and unit coefficients to K, prove invariant-subspace stability, and record the nonzero-subspace witness existence.\"},{\"id\":\"T006\",\"statement\":\"True\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T005\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S006\"],\"explanation\":\"Expand a selected nonzero vector in the established basis and prove existentially that at least one coordinate is nonzero.\"},{\"id\":\"T007\",\"statement\":\"True\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T005\",\"T006\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S007\"],\"explanation\":\"Apply each matrix unit to the chosen vector; divide by its nonzero coordinate to put every basis vector in W.\"},{\"id\":\"T008\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (K ⊗[ℤ] M) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.zM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T001\",\"T002\",\"T003\",\"T004\",\"T005\",\"T006\",\"T007\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"Discharge the zero/nonzero invariant-subspace cases and show the carrier nontrivial. This is the previous interface terminal and is NOT the original source-order target; an actual tensor-order bridge and source-facing assembly remain necessary.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T008\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T008\"}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":